WEBVTT

00:03.550 --> 00:06.120
What is the reason of my birth?

00:06.300 --> 00:10.230
Reason of my life, question of man.

00:10.240 --> 00:13.830
What he is?

00:14.020 --> 00:18.410
What he wants?

00:22.080 --> 00:29.490
Ima kimi ni mienai chikara ga osoi.
Now you are being troubled by an unseen power.

00:29.490 --> 00:34.560
Utsumuite namida kakushiteta.
You hang your head and hide your tears.

00:36.840 --> 00:43.820
Dou sureba ii ka? Sore sae wakarazu ni!
What should be done? That's unknown!

00:44.240 --> 00:51.690
Asphalt ni saku hana ni yuuki kanjita...
Blooming in the asphalt is a flower of courage...

00:53.490 --> 00:56.980
Itsumo kimi no soba ni iru yo.
We'll always be by your side.

00:57.200 --> 01:00.490
Da kara mou hitori ja nai.
So you're not alone anymore.

01:00.840 --> 01:04.340
Kimi ga michi ni mayou toki wa...
When you lose your way...

01:04.560 --> 01:07.920
Boku ga saki o aruku yo.
I'll walk ahead and lead you.

01:08.220 --> 01:11.750
Tooi sora koete...
Crossing to the far away sky...

01:11.950 --> 01:15.300
Bokura wa tobitatsu!
We're flying!

01:15.620 --> 01:19.140
Kitto soko ni aru...
It'll definitely be there...

01:19.140 --> 01:24.050
Sore ga kimi no yume
Your dream...

01:30.660 --> 01:35.300
Resurrected Jumbo

01:47.670 --> 01:48.890
Halt!

02:04.240 --> 02:07.210
You can't catch me that easily.

02:10.080 --> 02:11.040
Boss!

02:15.510 --> 02:17.090
Jeez!

02:28.630 --> 02:33.200
It doesn't matter! No matter how many times
you guys catch me, I'll escape!

02:36.370 --> 02:39.180
Skunk got arrested again.

02:39.200 --> 02:41.000
He never learns.

02:41.000 --> 02:42.030
I'm leaving.

02:42.030 --> 02:43.800
Your lunch!

02:43.820 --> 02:47.500
It's early Sunday morning.
Where are you going?

02:47.750 --> 02:48.910
Thank you.

02:49.080 --> 02:51.760
I'm going to Marine Park
with some friends.

02:51.780 --> 02:53.540
His teacher, Midori, is taking them.

02:53.540 --> 02:54.670
I see.

02:54.670 --> 02:55.660
See you later.

02:55.660 --> 02:57.220
-Have a good time!
-Take care.

02:58.690 --> 03:00.280
Marine Park.

03:21.680 --> 03:23.780
What are we doing next?

03:24.280 --> 03:25.990
What about the pipe slide?

03:25.990 --> 03:27.990
We already did that.

03:28.070 --> 03:30.380
I want to do it again.

03:32.320 --> 03:35.290
My balloon! My balloon!

03:37.690 --> 03:39.440
My balloon!

03:45.420 --> 03:46.810
What is that?

03:49.040 --> 03:49.740
Here you go.

03:49.740 --> 03:50.790
Thank you

03:52.300 --> 03:53.920
Good job, Atom!

03:53.950 --> 03:56.240
I'll be right back.

04:28.650 --> 04:30.580
Atom!

04:31.280 --> 04:35.410
Everyone went to the aquarium.

04:36.550 --> 04:39.730
Miss Midori, what is that big robot?

04:39.790 --> 04:41.500
That's Jumbo.

04:41.790 --> 04:45.930
Jumbo and I have been
good friends for a long time.

04:46.060 --> 04:47.550
Is that right?

04:47.970 --> 04:50.280
About 20 years ago...

04:50.340 --> 04:56.460
when the number of robots skyrocketed
the first robot expo was held here.

04:57.040 --> 04:59.870
It announced the arrival
of the robot age.

05:04.550 --> 05:09.750
Jumbo was created as a symbol of the expo.
He's the largest robot in the world.

05:10.560 --> 05:14.830
He was big and kind.
The kids loved him.

05:19.660 --> 05:22.570
I was chosen to give flowers
to Jumbo

05:22.570 --> 05:25.640
at the opening ceremony.

05:25.740 --> 05:28.310
Really? That's cool!

05:41.350 --> 05:48.630
Big, big
Robot Jumbo.

05:49.060 --> 05:56.470
We were Waiting for you.

05:56.830 --> 06:03.210
Strong and kind
Human friends.

06:03.240 --> 06:09.750
Let's build a wonderful future
Together.

06:26.960 --> 06:28.610
Thank you.

06:29.130 --> 06:31.920
Thank you, little girl.

06:40.080 --> 06:42.700
Even after the expo...

06:43.050 --> 06:47.040
...Jumbo remained here
as a monument.

06:47.990 --> 06:50.010
I used to live around here...

06:50.190 --> 06:53.770
...and he and I
have been friends for years.

06:58.100 --> 07:01.230
When I was feeling down or sad...

07:01.930 --> 07:04.310
...Jumbo was always there for me...

07:04.770 --> 07:07.290
...even though he doesn't
say anything.

07:17.550 --> 07:22.940
But when the new robots came out
people forgot about Jumbo.

07:24.390 --> 07:28.770
Jumbo was not taken care of,
and he got all rusty.

07:30.660 --> 07:34.620
But I'm still his friend.

07:38.040 --> 07:41.460
Jumbo? Are you talking about
that famous old robot?

07:41.460 --> 07:44.170
Have you heard of him?

07:44.240 --> 07:48.830
Of course.
He was popular during the expo.

07:48.950 --> 07:52.970
But after that,
he was forgotten and left alone.

07:53.150 --> 07:55.560
Poor thing.

07:57.020 --> 08:01.410
Dr. Ochanomizu, he's not alone.

08:29.050 --> 08:33.830
Welcome to Chroizier Prison
from which there is no escape.

08:33.870 --> 08:37.020
Detective Tawashi and Skunk.

08:37.060 --> 08:40.300
Warden, he is an escape artist.

08:40.330 --> 08:42.980
Please watch him like a hawk.

08:43.500 --> 08:45.160
No need to worry.

08:45.310 --> 08:50.910
No matter what kind of criminal he is,
he won't escape.

08:55.610 --> 08:58.190
You scumbag!
Take him to his cell!

09:01.920 --> 09:05.550
Getting out of here
will be a piece of cake.

09:10.260 --> 09:15.270
Let me repeat,
Skunk will do anything to escape.

09:15.300 --> 09:19.300
Please let us help you
guard the prison for a while.

09:19.450 --> 09:21.910
You worry too much.

09:22.010 --> 09:25.950
Chroizier Prison is on an island.
It's completely secure.

09:26.010 --> 09:29.100
Not even a cat could escape!

09:29.250 --> 09:33.860
But Skunk might use
a robot to break out.

09:33.920 --> 09:35.540
To guard against that

09:35.590 --> 09:41.150
we have a Guardian
Pulse that covers the whole island

09:41.490 --> 09:47.300
by interfering with
the robots' systems.

09:47.300 --> 09:51.900
This pulse paralyzes the robots' Al.

09:51.970 --> 09:55.020
Even a state-of-the-art robot
such as Atom will be powerless...

09:55.020 --> 09:58.360
...once he's on the prison grounds.
There's no need to worry.

09:59.180 --> 10:03.150
Once kids get new toys...

10:03.190 --> 10:05.390
...they forget about old ones.

10:05.480 --> 10:10.350
But me, I cherish the old things.

10:14.090 --> 10:19.290
Because of a low- pressure system,
a storm is expected tonight.

10:19.930 --> 10:23.220
Please be alert.
Coastal flooding is possible.

10:26.110 --> 10:27.650
I wonder what that is.

10:49.960 --> 10:51.370
Miss!

10:52.860 --> 10:56.020
It's too bad you saw that.

11:10.450 --> 11:11.960
What? What happened?

11:14.340 --> 11:15.390
Why is he doing this?

11:15.390 --> 11:17.710
What happened
to the Guardian Pulse?

11:39.290 --> 11:42.370
That's impossible!
Jumbo is at Chroizier Prison!

11:42.430 --> 11:44.770
Switch the picture to the prison.

11:44.770 --> 11:45.680
Yes, sir.

11:49.420 --> 11:51.350
My gosh.

12:00.630 --> 12:03.700
Can an old robot like this
do the job?

12:15.850 --> 12:18.750
The robot is bulletproof.

12:19.020 --> 12:22.350
Don't worry, boss.
We'll be right there.

12:27.910 --> 12:29.670
Stop Jumbo!

12:34.860 --> 12:38.110
Does the Guardian Pulse
affect the air car too?

12:43.520 --> 12:45.490
What's wrong with
the Guardian Pulse?

12:45.680 --> 12:47.500
It's working fine.

12:48.250 --> 12:49.860
Why--?

12:50.270 --> 12:52.910
Why isn't it stopping that robot?

12:55.980 --> 12:58.960
The latest Guardian Pulse
doesn't work on Jumbo...

12:58.990 --> 13:02.040
...an old robot with a simple system.

13:02.930 --> 13:05.860
Dr. Ochanomizu, what's going on?

13:05.910 --> 13:08.500
Atom,
In order to get Skunk out of prison,

13:08.500 --> 13:11.670
his men resurrected Jumbo.

13:11.730 --> 13:13.450
Resurrected Jumbo?

13:24.370 --> 13:26.980
Turn off the Guardian Pulse!

13:28.580 --> 13:29.570
Right now!

13:29.570 --> 13:31.080
What are we going to do, warden?

13:31.080 --> 13:32.240
Warden?

13:32.760 --> 13:36.940
There's no other way.
Turn off the Guardian Pulse.

13:37.030 --> 13:38.630
Yes, sir.

13:47.840 --> 13:49.430
Pardon the dust.

13:49.480 --> 13:53.760
We want the Guardian Pulse on.

13:56.030 --> 13:57.400
Where am I?

14:02.730 --> 14:05.170
Thanks for picking me up.

14:17.700 --> 14:19.480
My gosh.

14:19.770 --> 14:23.080
This state-of-the-art prison...

14:23.640 --> 14:28.290
...was defeated by an old robot.

14:29.350 --> 14:34.240
An old robot has its own merits.

14:34.620 --> 14:37.720
And the new one is here too.

14:38.660 --> 14:40.030
Atom!

14:40.360 --> 14:41.500
Guys!

14:42.090 --> 14:44.560
Don't worry. We'll be fine.

14:44.560 --> 14:45.720
Okay.

14:46.100 --> 14:49.640
I'm not going to let you use Jumbo
to help you commit crimes.

14:53.500 --> 14:59.870
I guess the Pulse works well
on new robots like Atom.

15:07.690 --> 15:12.330
Atom is paralyzed.
What a great device.

15:14.160 --> 15:15.700
I've got to do something.

15:22.900 --> 15:24.340
Get her--!

15:43.920 --> 15:45.930
Hold on!

15:45.930 --> 15:46.970
Right!

15:50.140 --> 15:51.510
You aren't getting away.

15:51.510 --> 15:53.230
Atom!

15:57.820 --> 15:59.610
Atom!

15:59.870 --> 16:01.130
Miss Midori!

16:04.910 --> 16:06.960
Help me, Atom!!

16:07.310 --> 16:08.850
Hey, Atom!

16:09.050 --> 16:14.300
Jumbo is not going to stop until
he destroys Metro City completely.

16:16.250 --> 16:18.620
Everyone, go after Skunk.

16:18.790 --> 16:22.590
I'll go after Jumbo.
Let's go to the docks.

16:37.780 --> 16:39.740
We'll stop Jumbo right here.

16:39.740 --> 16:41.390
Please wait!

16:43.880 --> 16:45.790
Please do not attack him!

16:45.790 --> 16:47.670
It's not Jumbo's fault.

16:47.670 --> 16:50.960
Get back! Look at what he's done.

16:51.060 --> 16:53.540
It's not Jumbo anymore.

16:57.110 --> 16:58.990
Ready. Fire!

17:04.440 --> 17:07.020
Stop! Jumbo!

17:15.110 --> 17:16.330
Atom!

17:20.590 --> 17:23.680
Stop, Jumbo!

17:25.390 --> 17:28.610
Wake up, Jumbo!

17:29.160 --> 17:34.920
You used to be friends with humans.

17:37.710 --> 17:38.610
Atom!

17:38.610 --> 17:40.440
Hold your fire!

17:50.450 --> 17:51.950
Jumbo!

17:55.880 --> 17:57.630
I'm running out of strength!

18:00.530 --> 18:02.050
Stop!

18:02.090 --> 18:04.610
Atom, get away!

18:05.880 --> 18:07.240
Miss!

18:10.400 --> 18:12.140
Don't, Jumbo.

18:12.140 --> 18:13.470
Miss Midori!

18:13.570 --> 18:15.060
Remember...

18:15.640 --> 18:19.130
...when you were
friends with humans?

18:19.310 --> 18:21.720
Jumbo, look at me!

18:22.550 --> 18:26.980
She's trying to appeal to his heart.

18:26.980 --> 18:30.250
Get into position!
Aim at his head!

18:30.250 --> 18:31.680
Atom!

18:37.960 --> 18:40.970
Dr. Ochanomizu, set off fireworks!

18:41.130 --> 18:42.620
Fireworks?

18:42.930 --> 18:46.710
We're going to bring back his
memories..

18:46.740 --> 18:48.740
of when he first met Midori.

18:48.940 --> 18:52.110
No, we can't get fireworks.

18:52.510 --> 18:53.590
Detective!

18:54.140 --> 18:56.280
I've got an idea.

18:56.850 --> 18:58.440
Listen, Jumbo.

18:59.120 --> 19:02.490
I've been your friend all these years.

19:30.410 --> 19:31.860
Miss Midori!

19:34.950 --> 19:37.120
Big,

19:37.650 --> 19:39.450
Big,

19:40.690 --> 19:43.640
Robot Jumbo.

19:45.260 --> 19:47.560
We were

19:47.970 --> 19:53.370
Waiting for you

19:53.500 --> 20:00.650
Strong and kind Human friends.

20:00.810 --> 20:04.190
Let's build a wonderful future,

20:04.410 --> 20:08.610
Together

20:23.330 --> 20:26.210
You created the fireworks
with lasers.

20:26.340 --> 20:29.270
I hope it'll work.

20:42.590 --> 20:44.000
Jumbo.

20:46.720 --> 20:53.220
Jumbo's circuits were programmed
to react to the lights.

20:53.270 --> 20:57.910
Looks like we were able
to turn the old memory on.

21:02.740 --> 21:07.390
Thank you, little girl.

21:17.190 --> 21:19.010
Isn't it amazing!

21:19.050 --> 21:20.720
Wait! Wait!

21:27.760 --> 21:30.170
I'm glad Jumbo is back to his old self.

21:30.200 --> 21:32.380
We owe Dr. Ochanomizu a lot.

21:32.930 --> 21:36.990
The Ministry of Science
took over the care of Jumbo...

21:37.070 --> 21:39.660
...and now kids can play with him.

21:41.480 --> 21:45.180
Now Jumbo
has a lot of friends.

21:45.650 --> 21:47.430
He looks happy.

21:48.500 --> 21:51.490
I don't think Jumbo was ever lonely...

21:51.860 --> 21:55.100
...because he always had you,
Miss Midori.

22:11.950 --> 22:17.480
Naze... Naze... Kokoro ga...
Why... Why... is my heart...

22:17.880 --> 22:23.090
Itamu to namida ni naru?
Is filled with pain and tears?

22:23.470 --> 22:28.980
Naze... Naze... Namida ga...
Why... Why... Tears...

22:29.260 --> 22:34.560
Ochiru to Hitori ni naru.
They fall and I'm alone.

22:34.920 --> 22:40.200
Chiisa na hiza kakae...
I hold my tiny knees...

22:40.680 --> 22:48.840
Tooku wo mata miageru.
And look up and far away.

22:49.240 --> 22:52.120
Hiroi... Hiroi...
Vast... Vast...

22:52.330 --> 23:00.330
Kono sora yori motto hiroi hazu da!
It has to be more wide than these skies!

23:00.920 --> 23:03.330
Takai... Takai...
High... High...

23:03.760 --> 23:12.040
Ano kumo yori motto takai hazu da!
It has to be higher than those clouds!

23:12.340 --> 23:17.070
Kimi no kokoro mo...
Your heart is...

23:23.650 --> 23:25.000
I'm Uran!

23:25.090 --> 23:27.590
I was just born!

23:27.720 --> 23:30.190
Wait for me, big brother Atom!

23:30.450 --> 23:32.700
Next time :
Birth of Uran.

23:32.760 --> 23:35.730
With your heart, catch the future!
